      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote",
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Base Image Generator (SDXL)\n\nSame two-stage shape as **CNC_Image_Creater**, running SDXL 1.0 base instead of FLUX.2 Klein.\n\n**Stage 1** runs on its own. **Stage 2 starts muted.**\n\n## How to use\n1. Run. Look at the **Stage 1** image.\n2. Not happy? Run again (seed is on `randomize`).\n3. Happy? Set the Stage 1 **KSampler** `control_after_generate` to **`fixed`** so Stage 1 reproduces the same image instead of a new one.\n4. Select the **STAGE 2** group by its title bar and press **Ctrl+M** to unmute.\n5. Adjust the Stage 2 prompt and `denoise`, then Run.\n\n## How this differs from the Klein workflow\n- **The negative prompt is real here.** SDXL runs at CFG 7, so everything in the negative box actually gets pushed away. That is your best tool against branches, ground planes and shadows.\n- **Stage 2 is true img2img** with a `denoise` slider, not reference-latent conditioning. `denoise` *is* the strength dial: 0.3 = light touch-up, 0.5 = rework the background but keep the pose, 0.8 = nearly a new image.\n- **30 steps, not 4.** SDXL is not distilled, so expect ~30-60s a frame instead of seconds.\n\n## Which one to use\nKlein gives better prompt adherence and photoreal detail in a fraction of the time. Reach for SDXL when you want the negative prompt as a blunt instrument, or a stylised / illustrative look rather than a photograph.\n\n---\n\n## Saving is OFF by default\n\nEvery image lands in a **Preview Image** node. Nothing is written to `ComfyUI/output` unless you deliberately save it.\n\n### To keep an image\n1. Set the sampler's `control_after_generate` to **`fixed`** (locks the seed).\n2. Type a descriptive name into the **Save Image** node's `filename_prefix` - replace `RENAME_BEFORE_SAVING`.\n3. Select the **Save Image** node and press **Ctrl+M** to unmute it.\n4. Run. The seed is locked so nothing regenerates - ComfyUI serves the cached image and just writes the file.\n5. **Ctrl+M it back to muted** before your next exploration round.\n\nThe Save Image nodes sit *outside* the coloured groups on purpose, so muting or unmuting a stage never switches saving on behind your back.\n\n### Naming\n`subject_pose_variant` - e.g. `raven_sideprofile_flatbg_A`, `skull_frontal_deepcut_B`. No spaces. The name follows the file all the way to the STL and the g-code, so make it mean something."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
    {
      "id": 51,
      "type": "MarkdownNote",
      "pos": [
        500,
        1290
      ],
      "size": [
